          %h2#idea Idea
          %p
            For
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi p
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} p
            a
            = succeed "," do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/prime+number"} prime number
            %em Steenrod algebra
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi 𝒜
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \mathcal{A}
            is the
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/associative+algebra"} associative algebra
            over the
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/prime+field"} prime field
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %msub
                    %mi 𝔽
                    %mi p
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \mathbb{F}_p
            of
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/cohomology+operations"} cohomology operations
            on
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/ordinary+cohomology"} ordinary cohomology
            with
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/coefficients"} coefficients
            in
            = succeed "." do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %msub
                      %mi 𝔽
                      %mi p
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \mathbb{F}_p
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi p
                  %mo =
                  %mn 2
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} p = 2
            this is the
            = succeed "-algebra" do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %msub
                      %mi 𝔽
                      %mn 2
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \mathbb{F}_2
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Steenrod+square"} Steenrod square
            operations. (This case
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi p
                  %mo =
                  %mn 2
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} p = 2
            is often understood by default.)
          %p
            For any
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/prime+number"} prime
            = succeed "," do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi p
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} p
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi p
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} p
            Steenrod algebra furthermore has the structure of a
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Hopf+algebra"} Hopf algebra
            over
            = succeed "," do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %msub
                      %mi 𝔽
                      %mi p
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \mathbb{F}_p
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/linear+duals"} linear duals
            this gives the
            = succeed "," do
              %em dual Steenrod algebra
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %msub
                    %mi 𝒜
                    %mo *
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \mathcal{A}_\ast
            instead of
            = succeed "." do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %msup
                      %mi 𝒜
                      %mo *
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \mathcal{A}^\ast
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Hopf+algebra"} Hopf algebra
            over
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %msub
                    %mi 𝔽
                    %mi p
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \mathbb{F}_p
            that is commutative, but non-co-commutative.
          %p
            The dual
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %msub
                    %mi 𝔽
                    %mi p
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \mathbb{F}_p
            Steenrod algebra is a special case of a
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/commutative+Hopf+algebroid"} commutative Hopf algebroid
            structure canonically induced on the self
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/generalized+homology"} generalized homology
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
