            = succeed ")" do
              %a{:href => "#Lurie07"} Lurie 07
          %h3#for_generalized_cohomology For generalized cohomology
          %p
            The Steenrod algebra and its standard properties, such as the
            = succeed "," do
              %a{:href => "#OnAdemRelations"} Adem relations
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Cotor"} Cotor
            groups of
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/comodules"} comodules
            over any
            = succeed "." do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/commutative+Hopf+algebroid"} commutative Hopf algebroid
          %p
            This is due to (
            %a{:href => "#May70"}> May 70, 11.8
            ). A review is in (
            %a{:href => "#Ravenel"}> Ravenel, appendix 1, theorem A1.5.2
            ).
          %p
            In particular for
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi E
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} E
            a suitable
            = succeed "," do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/E-infinity+ring"} E-infinity ring
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/generalized+homology"} generalized homology
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %msub
                    %mi E
                    %mo •
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                  %mi E
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} E_\bullet(E)
            forms a (graded-)
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/commutative+Hopf+algebroid"} commutative Hopf algebroid
            over
            = succeed "." do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %msub
                      %mi E
                      %mo •
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} E_\bullet
          %p
            See at
            %em
              %a{:href => "#HopfAlgebroidstructureForGeneralized"} Hopf algebroid structure – For generalized cohomology
            below. For more see at
            = succeed "." do
              %em
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Adams+spectral+sequence"} Adams spectral sequence
                –
                %a{:href => "Adams+spectral+sequence#FirstPageAndHopfAlgebroid"} The first page
          %h2#properties Properties
          %h3#presentation_by_generators_and_relations Presentation by generators and relations
          #SerreCartanBasis.num_defn
            %h6#definition_2 Definition
            %p
              The
              %em Serre-Cartan basis
              is the
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/subset"} subset
              of elements of the Steenrod algebra on those of the form
            .maruku-equation
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "block", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %msup
                      %mi Sq
                      %mrow
                        %msub
                          %mi i
                          %mn 1
                    %mo ∘
                    %msup
                      %mi Sq
                      %mrow
                        %msub
                          %mi i
                          %mn 2
                    %mo ∘
                    %mi ⋯
                    %mo ∘
                    %msup
                      %mi Sq
                      %mrow
                        %msub
                          %mi i
                          %mi n
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"}
                    Sq^{i_1} \circ Sq^{i_2} \circ \cdots \circ Sq^{i_n}
            %p
              where
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %msub
                      %mi i
                      %mi k
                    %mo ∈
                    %mi ℕ
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} i_k \in \mathbb{N}
              subject to the relation
            .maruku-equation
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "block", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %msub
                      %mi i
                      %mi k
                    %mo ≥
                    %mn 2
                    %msub
                      %mi i
                      %mrow
                        %mi k
                        %mo +
                        %mn 1
                    %mo .
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"}
                    i_k \geq 2 i_{k+1}.
          %p
            This is indeed a
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/linear+basis"} linear basis
            for the
            = succeed "-" do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %msub
                      %mi 𝔽
                      %mn 2
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \mathbb{F}_2
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/vector+space"} vector space
            underlying the Steenrod algebra.
          #AdemRelations.num_prop
            %h6#proposition Proposition
            %p
              The
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Steenrod+square"} Steenrod square
              operations satisfy the following relation, for all for all
              = succeed ":" do
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %mn 0
                      %mo &lt;
                      %mi i
                      %mo &lt;
                      %mn 2
                      %mi j
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} 0 \lt i \lt 2 j
            .maruku-equation
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "block", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %msup
                      %mi Sq
                      %mi i
                    %mo ∘
                    %msup
                      %mi Sq
                      %mi j
                    %mo =
                    %munderover
                      %mo{:lspace => "thinmathspace", :rspace => "thinmathspace"} ∑
                      %mrow
                        %mi k
                        %mo =
                        %mn 0
                      %mrow
                        %mo{:stretchy => "false"} [
                        %mi i
                        %mo{:stretchy => "false"} /
                        %mn 2
                        %mo{:stretchy => "false"} ]
                    %msub
                      %mrow
                        %mo (
                        %mrow
                          %mtable
                            %mtr
                              %mtd
                                %mi j
                                %mo −
                                %mi k
                                %mo −
                                %mn 1
                            %mtr
                              %mtd
                                %mi i
                                %mo −
                                %mn 2
                                %mi k
                        %mo )
                      %mrow
                        %mi mod
                        %mn 2
                    %msup
                      %mi Sq
                      %mrow
                        %mi i
                        %mo +
                        %mi j
                        %mo −
                        %mi k
                    %mo ∘
                    %msup
                      %mi Sq
                      %mi k
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"}
                    Sq^i \circ Sq^j
                    \=
                    \\sum_{k = 0}^{[i/2]}
                    \\left(
                    \\array{
                    j - k - 1
                    \\\
                    i - 2k
                    }
                    \\right)_{mod 2}
                    Sq^{i + j -k} \circ Sq^k
          %p
            These are called the
            %strong Ádem relations
            (
            %a{:href => "#Adem52"}> Ádem 52
            ).
          .num_prop
            %h6#proposition_2 Proposition
            %p
              The Ádam relations precisely generate the
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/ideal"} ideal
              of relations among the Serre-Cartan basis elements, def.
              = succeed "," do
                %a.maruku-ref{:href => "#AdemRelations"}
          %p
            More generally, for other
            = succeed ":" do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/prime+numbers"} prime numbers
          #SteenrodAlgebraForHFp.num_defn
            %h6#definition_3 Definition
            %p
              Let
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi p
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} p
              be a
              = succeed "." do
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/prime+number"} prime number
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %msub
                      %mi 𝔽
                      %mi p
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \mathbb{F}_p
              for the corresponding
              = succeed "." do
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/prime+field"} prime field
            %p
              The
              %strong
                mod
                = succeed "-Steenrod" do
                  %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                    %semantics
                      %mrow
                        %mi p
                      %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} p
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %msub
                      %mi 𝒜
                      %mrow
                        %msub
                          %mi 𝔽
                          %mi p
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \mathcal{A}_{\mathbb{F}_p}
              is the graded co-commutative
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Hopf+algebra"} Hopf algebra
              over
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %msub
                      %mi 𝔽
                      %mi p
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \mathbb{F}_p
              which is
            %ul
              %li
                %p
                  for
                  %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                    %semantics
                      %mrow
                        %mi p
                        %mo =
                        %mn 2
                      %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} p = 2
                  generated by elements denoted
                  %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                    %semantics
                      %mrow
                        %msup
                          %mi Sq
                          %mi n
                      %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} Sq^n
                  for
                  = succeed "," do
                    %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                      %semantics
                        %mrow
                          %mi n
                          %mo ∈
                          %mi ℕ
                        %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} n \in \mathbb{N}
                  = succeed ";" do
                    %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                      %semantics
                        %mrow
                          %mi n
                          %mo ≥
                          %mn 1
                        %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} n \geq 1
              %li
                %p
                  for
                  %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                    %semantics
                      %mrow
                        %mi p
                        %mo &gt;
                        %mn 2
                      %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} p \gt 2
                  generated by elements denoted
                  %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                    %semantics
                      %mrow
                        %mi β
                      %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \beta
                  and
                  %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                    %semantics
                      %mrow
                        %msup
                          %mi P
                          %mi n
                      %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} P^n
                  for
                  = succeed "," do
                    %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                      %semantics
                        %mrow
                          %mi n
                          %mo ∈
                          %mi ℕ
                        %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} n \in \mathbb{N}
                  %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                    %semantics
                      %mrow
                        %mi n
                        %mo ≥
                        %mn 1
                      %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} n \geq 1
            %p
              (called the
              = succeed ")" do
                %strong Serre-Cartan basis elements
              = succeed "):" do
                %strong Ádem relations
            %p
              %strong>
                for
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %mi p
                      %mo =
                      %mn 2
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} p = 2
              \:
            %p
              for
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mn 0
                    %mo &lt;
                    %mi h
                    %mo &lt;
                    %mn 2
                    %mi k
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} 0 \lt h \lt 2k
              the
            .maruku-equation
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "block", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %msup
                      %mi Sq
                      %mi h
                    %msup
                      %mi Sq
                      %mi k
                    %mspace{:width => "thickmathspace"}
                    %mo =
                    %mspace{:width => "thickmathspace"}
                    %munderover
                      %mo{:lspace => "thinmathspace", :rspace => "thinmathspace"} ∑
                      %mrow
                        %mi i
                        %mo =
                        %mn 0
                      %mrow
                        %mo{:stretchy => "false"} [
                        %mi h
                        %mo{:stretchy => "false"} /
                        %mn 2
                        %mo{:stretchy => "false"} ]
                    %mrow
                      %mo (
                      %mrow
                        %mtable
                          %mtr
                            %mtd
                              %mi k
                              %mo −
                              %mi i
                              %mo −
                              %mn 1
                          %mtr
                            %mtd
                              %mi h
                              %mo −
                              %mn 2
                              %mi i
                      %mo )
                    %msup
                      %mi Sq
                      %mrow
                        %mi h
                        %mo +
                        %mi k
                        %mo −
                        %mi i
                    %msup
                      %mi Sq
                      %mi i
                    %mspace{:width => "thinmathspace"}
                    %mo ,
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"}
                    Sq^h Sq^k
                    \\;=\;
                    \\underoverset{i = 0}{[h/2]}{\sum}
                    \\left(
                    \\array{
                    k -i - 1
                    \\\
                    h - 2i
                    }
                    \\right)
                    Sq^{h + k -i} Sq^i
                    \\,,
            %p
              %strong>
                for
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %mi p
                      %mo &gt;
                      %mn 2
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} p \gt 2
              \:
            %p
              for
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mn 0
                    %mo &lt;
                    %mi h
                    %mo &lt;
                    %mi p
                    %mi k
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} 0 \lt h \lt p k
              then
            .maruku-equation
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "block", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %msup
                      %mi P
                      %mi h
                    %msup
                      %mi P
                      %mi k
                    %mspace{:width => "thickmathspace"}
                    %mo =
                    %mspace{:width => "thickmathspace"}
                    %munderover
                      %mo{:lspace => "thinmathspace", :rspace => "thinmathspace"} ∑
                      %mrow
                        %mi i
                        %mo =
                        %mn 0
                      %mrow
                        %mo{:stretchy => "false"} [
                        %mi h
                        %mo{:stretchy => "false"} /
                        %mi p
                        %mo{:stretchy => "false"} ]
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %mo{:lspace => "verythinmathspace", :rspace => "0em"} −
                    %mn 1
                    %msup
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                      %mrow
                        %mi h
                        %mo +
                        %mi i
                    %mrow
                      %mo (
                      %mrow
                        %mtable
                          %mtr
                            %mtd
                              %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                              %mi p
                              %mo −
                              %mn 1
                              %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                              %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                              %mi k
                              %mo −
                              %mi i
                              %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                              %mo −
                              %mn 1
                          %mtr
                            %mtd
                              %mi h
                              %mo −
                              %mi p
                              %mi i
                      %mo )
                    %msup
                      %mi P
                      %mrow
                        %mi h
                        %mo +
                        %mi k
                        %mo −
                        %mi i
                    %msup
                      %mi P
                      %mi i
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"}
                    P^h P^k
                    \\;=\;
                    \\underoverset{i = 0}{[h/p]}{\sum}
                    (-1)^{h+i}
                    \\left(
                    \\array{
                    (p-1)(k-i) - 1
                    \\\
                    h - p i
                    }
                    \\right)
                    P^{h +k - i}P^i
            %p
              and if
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mn 0
                    %mo &lt;
                    %mi h
                    %mo ≤
                    %mi p
                    %mi k
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} 0 \lt h \le p k
              then
            .maruku-equation
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "block", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mrow
                      %mtable{:columnalign => "right left right left right left right left right left", :columnspacing => "0em", :displaystyle => "true"}
                        %mtr
                          %mtd
                            %msup
                              %mi P
                              %mi h
                            %mi β
                            %msup
                              %mi P
                              %mi k
                          %mtd
                            %mo =
                            %mspace{:width => "thickmathspace"}
                            %munderover
                              %mo{:lspace => "thinmathspace", :rspace => "thinmathspace"} ∑
                              %mrow
                                %mo{:stretchy => "false"} [
