                )
              %p
                Lecture 5
                %em The Adem relations (cont.)
                (
                %a{:href => "http://ocw.mit.edu/courses/mathematics/18-917-topics-in-algebraic-topology-the-sullivan-conjecture-fall-2007/lecture-notes/lecture5.pdf"}> pdf
                )
          %p The general algebraic approach was laid out in:
          %ul
            %li#May70
              %p
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Peter+May"}> Peter May
                ,
                = succeed "," do
                  %em A general algebraic approach to Steenrod operations
                %em The Steenrod Algebra and its Applications
                (Proc. Conf. to Celebrate N. E. Steenrod’s Sixtieth Birthday, Battelle Memorial Inst., Columbus, Ohio, 1970), Lecture Notes in Mathematics, Vol. 168, Springer, Berlin, 1970, pp. 153–231. (
                %a{:href => "http://www.math.uchicago.edu/~may/BOOKS/Algebraic.pdf"}> pdf
                )
            %li#BrunerMayMcLureSteinberger86
              %p
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Robert+Bruner"}> Robert Bruner
                ,
                = succeed "," do
                  %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Peter+May"} Peter May
                = succeed "," do
                  %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/James+McClure"} James McClure
                = succeed "," do
                  %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Mark+Steinberger"} Mark Steinberger
                = succeed "," do
                  %em
                    %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}>
                      %semantics
                        %mrow
                          %msub
                            %mi H
                            %mn ∞
                        %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} H_\infty
                    \-Ring Spectra and their Applications
                = succeed "," do
                  %strong 1176
                = succeed "," do
                  %a{:href => "https://link.springer.com/book/10.1007/BFb0075405"} doi:10.1007/BFb0075405
                = succeed "&rbrack;" do
                  %a{:href => "http://www.math.uchicago.edu/~may/BOOKS/h_infty.pdf"} pdf
          %p
            reviewed by
            = succeed "." do
              %a{:href => "#Ravenel"} Ravenel 1986, A1.5
          %p Further textbook accounts:
          %ul
            %li
              %p
                Harvey Margolis:
                = succeed "," do
                  %em Spectra and the Steenrod algebra
            %li#Kochmann96
              %p
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Stanley+Kochmann"}> Stanley Kochmann
                , section 2.5 of
                = succeed "," do
                  %em
                    %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Bordism%2C+Stable+Homotopy+and+Adams+Spectral+Sequences"} Bordism, Stable Homotopy and Adams Spectral Sequences
            %li#Schwede12
              %p
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Stefan+Schwede"}> Stefan Schwede
                , chapter II section 10 of
                %em
                  %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Symmetric+spectra"} Symmetric spectra
                (2012) &amp;lbrack;
                %a{:href => "http://www.math.uni-bonn.de/~schwede/SymSpec-v3.pdf"}> pdf
                \&amp;rbrack;
          %p Lecture notes:
          %ul
            %li#Rognes12
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/John+Rognes"}> John Rognes
              , section 3 of:
              %em The Adams spectral sequence
              (2012) &amp;lbrack;
              %a{:href => "http://folk.uio.no/rognes/papers/notes.050612.pdf"}> pdf
              \&amp;rbrack;
          %p Further review:
          %ul
            %li#Ravenel
              %p
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Doug+Ravenel"}> Doug Ravenel
                ,
                %em
                  %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Complex+cobordism+and+stable+homotopy+groups+of+spheres"} Complex cobordism and stable homotopy groups of spheres
                Academic Press (1986)
              %blockquote
                %p (appendix 1, section 5 reviews the abstract algebraic definition).
            %li
              %p
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Agn%C3%A8s+Beaudry"}> Agnès Beaudry
                ,
                = succeed "," do
                  %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Jonathan+A.+Campbell"} Jonathan A. Campbell
                = succeed "," do
                  %em A Guide for Computing Stable Homotopy Groups
                = succeed "," do
                  %em Topology and Quantum Theory in Interaction
                = succeed "," do
                  %strong 718
                = succeed "," do
                  %a{:href => "https://arxiv.org/abs/1801.07530"} arXiv:1801.07530
                = succeed "&rbrack;" do
                  %a{:href => "https://bookstore.ams.org/view?ProductCode=CONM/718"} ams:conm/718
              %blockquote
                %p
                  (with an eye towards
                  = succeed ")" do
                    %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/functorial+quantum+field+theory"} functorial quantum field theory
            %li
              %p
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Cary+Malkiewich"}> Cary Malkiewich
                ,
                %em The Steenrod Algebra
                \&amp;lbrack;
                %a{:href => "https://people.math.binghamton.edu/malkiewich/steenrod.pdf"}> pdf
                ,
                = succeed "&rbrack;" do
                  %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/files/Malkiewich-SteenrodAlgebra.pdf", :title => "pdf"} pdf
            %li
              %p
                Wikipedia:
                %em
                  %a{:href => "https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Steenrod_algebra"} Steenrod algebra
          %p On the dual Steenrod algebra:
          %ul
            %li
              J. Palmieri,
              %em Some quotient Hopf algebras of the dual Steenrod algebra
              (
              %a{:href => "http://www.math.washington.edu/~palmieri/Papers/quotient.pdf"}> pdf
              )
          %p For a commented list of furhter references see also
          %ul
            %li
              %em
                %a{:href => "http://www.math.uwo.ca/~sisaacso/steenrod-seminar/steenrod.xhtml"} Steenrod algebra learning seminar
          %p See also
          %ul
            %li
              %a{:href => "http://math.berkeley.edu/~aaron/adem/"} online Adem relation calculator
          %h3#ReferencesHopfAlgebroid
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}>
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %msub
                    %mi E
                    %mo •
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} E_\bullet
            \-Hopf algebroid structure
          %p
            The
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/commutative+Hopf+algebroid"} commutative Hopf algebroid
            structure on the dual
            = succeed "-Steenrod" do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi E
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} E
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %msub
                    %mi E
                    %mo •
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                  %mi E
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} E_\bullet(E)
            and its relation to the
            = succeed "-term" do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %msup
                      %mi E
                      %mn 2
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} E^2
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Adams+spectral+sequence"} Adams spectral sequence
            is discussed in
          %ul
            %li#Baker
              %p
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Andrew+Baker"}> Andrew Baker
                ,
                = succeed "," do
                  %em Brave new Hopf algebroids
                %a{:href => "http://www.maths.gla.ac.uk/~ajb/dvi-ps/brave-ha.pdf"} pdf
            %li#BakerLazarev01
              %p
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Andrew+Baker"}> Andrew Baker
                ,
                = succeed "," do
                  %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Andrey+Lazarev"} Andrey Lazarev
                = succeed "," do
                  %em On the Adams Spectral Sequence for R-modules
                = succeed ")" do
                  %a{:href => "http://arxiv.org/abs/math/0105079"} arXiv:math/0105079
            %li#BakerJeanneret02
              %p
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Andrew+Baker"} Andrew Baker
                and Alain Jeanneret,
                = succeed "," do
                  %em
                    Brave new Hopf algebroids and extensions of
                    = succeed "-algebras" do
                      %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                        %semantics
